  "note": "Breaker's 2-lap budget both found real defects: lap 1 was severe data loss (a real pre-existing GDM AutomaticLogin setting was permanently destroyed by uninstall's new .bak-delete-on-success; fixed by extracting and restoring the backup's original AutomaticLogin*/AutomaticLoginEnable content surgically, not a wholesale file restore) plus a return-code bug; lap 2 found a lower-probability unreadable-backup data-loss path (fail-closed now) plus an unbounded duplicate-restore bug on repeated calls. All fixed and gate re-verified, no lap 3. Reviewer found 3 more non-blocking follow-ups (enable_autologin's cp -a backup write is still non-atomic; a two-[daemon]-header edge case; a now-3x-duplicated regex) -- could NOT file these as GitHub issues, the token lacks issues:write scope (403 on attempt despite read access working); recorded in the commit message and CHECKPOINT archive instead, owner needs to file by hand or grant the scope. Pre-existing unrelated Java boot-test failure (VK_A -> evdev 30) reconfirmed to reproduce on a clean tree, owned by the separate fix-boottests-evdev-keycodes line. No CI workflows configured in this repo; the local gate (run-tests.sh) was the only check.",
